# The build context is an allow-list: everything is excluded, and only what
# `go build ./cmd/sherlock` reads is admitted. A deny-list admits every new
# file at the root until someone remembers to exclude it, which is how a
# credential reached the build stage in #594 and how the compiled tool
# binaries reached it in #597.
#
# The re-includes are directories rather than globs on purpose:
# internal/agent/instructions.go embeds ego.md, so a `*.go` allow-list would
# drop an embedded asset and break the build.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd
!internal

# Final deny, placed after the re-includes because the last matching pattern
# wins: a credential stays out of the context whatever a later re-include
# admits (#594).
.env
.env.*
